WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.167 --> 00:00:03.903
Okay.
He is Professor of Marketing
at NYU Stern School,

00:00:03.903 --> 00:00:06.573
and this is the host of the
<i>Prof G Pod with Scott Galloway.</i>

00:00:06.673 --> 00:00:08.474
Scott Galloway is back with us.

00:00:08.675 --> 00:00:11.811
-(AUDIENCE APPLAUDING)
-How are you?

00:00:12.445 --> 00:00:15.214
Okay. She's a co-host of
<i> The Five</i> on<i> Fox News,</i>

00:00:15.315 --> 00:00:17.416
and head of research
at Bustle, Jessica Tarlov.

00:00:17.516 --> 00:00:19.018
Jessica, how are you doing?

00:00:19.452 --> 00:00:21.788
-Finally got you here.
-Yes.

00:00:22.822 --> 00:00:24.690
Okay. So I wanna start off
with this.

00:00:24.790 --> 00:00:26.625
Mike Johnson.
I know everyone is saying

00:00:26.792 --> 00:00:28.527
"Mike Johnson,
my insurance agent?"

00:00:28.694 --> 00:00:30.663
(LAUGHTER)

00:00:31.130 --> 00:00:32.298
No, the other Mike Johnson.

00:00:32.431 --> 00:00:34.033
He's the Speaker of the House
now.

00:00:34.600 --> 00:00:37.069
So, I've been using this phrase,
"slow-moving coup,"

00:00:37.370 --> 00:00:40.106
about Trump since before
he got elected the first time.

00:00:40.406 --> 00:00:41.474
And a lot of people
were laughing.

00:00:41.574 --> 00:00:43.075
I see a lot of people
use it now.

00:00:43.709 --> 00:00:45.411
And every time we
don't completely lose

00:00:45.511 --> 00:00:47.112
our way of government,
somebody says,

00:00:47.179 --> 00:00:49.649
"Oh, well where's your
slow-moving coup now?"

00:00:50.016 --> 00:00:53.252
It's slow.
That's my answer. It's slow.

00:00:53.319 --> 00:00:55.455
But this--
what happened this week--

00:00:55.555 --> 00:00:59.459
I remember I did a very
dark editorial like 2022,

00:00:59.592 --> 00:01:01.895
like the last one of the year
after that election, saying--

00:01:02.061 --> 00:01:03.730
because we all thought the
Republicans were going to win--

00:01:03.863 --> 00:01:05.097
and I said,
what's going to happen

00:01:05.231 --> 00:01:08.534
is that the people who
were not in place in 2020

00:01:08.768 --> 00:01:11.304
that Trump tried to get his
bidding to overturn elections,

00:01:11.437 --> 00:01:13.673
the John Raffenspergers
of the world, who said,

00:01:13.773 --> 00:01:15.875
"No, I can't find you votes."

00:01:16.842 --> 00:01:19.712
They're all gonna get replaced,
and it didn't happen then.

00:01:20.180 --> 00:01:24.017
But, that's kind of happening
now with Mike Johnson,

00:01:24.117 --> 00:01:27.954
the ultimate election denier,
and now all the Republicans,

00:01:28.087 --> 00:01:30.289
it took them 22 days
to get this guy.

00:01:31.157 --> 00:01:33.626
But now they finally got
the guy who's Trump's guy.

00:01:33.726 --> 00:01:37.663
You know, it takes time to get
your people, to infiltrate them
into these positions.

00:01:37.963 --> 00:01:41.600
But I'm sorry, I think
that thesis still holds.

00:01:41.667 --> 00:01:43.069
And I think,
is this the moment--

00:01:43.202 --> 00:01:44.370
let me ask you the question,

00:01:44.670 --> 00:01:47.506
the Republican party is just
the MAGA party now, right?

00:01:47.639 --> 00:01:48.541
This--

00:01:49.208 --> 00:01:50.109
I think so.

00:01:50.242 --> 00:01:51.677
I felt that way for a while,

00:01:51.777 --> 00:01:53.979
and there were a few
kind of glimmers,

00:01:54.079 --> 00:01:57.816
and I think Kevin McCarthy
was like this fancy shiny object

00:01:57.950 --> 00:01:59.152
that a lot of people thought--

00:01:59.252 --> 00:02:01.087
(CHUCKLES) Never heard him
described that way, but...

00:02:01.220 --> 00:02:02.521
-(LAUGHTER)
-JESSICA TARLOV: Well...

00:02:02.688 --> 00:02:03.822
He's handsome, he's charming.

00:02:03.956 --> 00:02:06.526
He's the number one Republican
fundraiser out there, right?

00:02:06.659 --> 00:02:08.694
Even in the last quarter,
he raised 14 million dollars.

00:02:08.828 --> 00:02:12.798
He's the Nancy Pelosi
of the other side
in terms of raising money.

00:02:12.898 --> 00:02:13.766
BILL: Wow.

00:02:13.966 --> 00:02:16.468
-Well...
-(STAMMERING) I-- I don't--

00:02:16.602 --> 00:02:18.204
This is a side of him
I never thought of.

00:02:18.304 --> 00:02:19.538
Well, that's what
I'm here to deliver.

00:02:19.639 --> 00:02:20.540
BILL: I see.

00:02:20.640 --> 00:02:22.976
-(AUDIENCE LAUGHS, APPLAUDS)
-No. I just--

00:02:23.142 --> 00:02:27.680
having spent a lot of time
in the conservative ecosystem,

00:02:27.780 --> 00:02:29.449 line:0%
-these are things that I
pay attention to.
-BILL: Right.

00:02:29.549 --> 00:02:31.984 line:0%
Why is this one more useful than
this one, for instance.

00:02:32.118 --> 00:02:35.655 line:0%
And Kevin McCarthy
comes off as someone normal.

00:02:35.821 --> 00:02:36.955 line:0%
He is not normal, right?

00:02:37.089 --> 00:02:39.659 line:0%
He's someone who had a day
where he said, you know,

00:02:39.759 --> 00:02:41.794 line:0%
Donald Trump is responsible
for January 6th.

00:02:41.894 --> 00:02:43.662
And the next day,
he was at Mar-a-Lago,

00:02:43.796 --> 00:02:45.931
throwing back martinis
and hanging out with the crew.

00:02:46.064 --> 00:02:47.433
-So--
-(CHUCKLES) Yeah.

00:02:48.167 --> 00:02:51.571
But this guy also has
a sheen to him, right?

00:02:51.704 --> 00:02:53.105
He doesn't present
like what you would think.

00:02:53.172 --> 00:02:55.407
Last week, we thought it was
going to be Jim Jordan, right?

00:02:55.507 --> 00:02:59.879
Has no proper clothes, you know,
sits like this. Whatever.

00:02:59.945 --> 00:03:03.449
And then, we get this guy
who's a lawyer,

00:03:03.816 --> 00:03:07.987
who has a long career
of going after these
kind of social issues.

00:03:08.087 --> 00:03:09.856
You already mentioned it
in the monologue,

00:03:10.089 --> 00:03:13.159
about the sodomy laws,
criminalizing homosexuality.

00:03:13.259 --> 00:03:15.728
He was-- In the election
integrity front,

00:03:15.828 --> 00:03:17.630
he wasn't just someone
who signed on.

00:03:17.730 --> 00:03:21.033
He was an architect of the plan
to get our votes thrown out

00:03:21.133 --> 00:03:22.401
in Pennsylvania and Georgia

00:03:22.501 --> 00:03:23.603
-and Michigan.
-BILL: Yeah.

00:03:24.470 --> 00:03:26.606
He is so much more frightening
in that sense.

00:03:26.706 --> 00:03:29.008
But I do think, and obviously,

00:03:29.175 --> 00:03:31.276
want to hear what you guys
think about this as well,

00:03:31.376 --> 00:03:33.279
I think it is a good thing
for Democrats

00:03:33.479 --> 00:03:34.747
that he was made Speaker,

00:03:34.881 --> 00:03:37.049
because everything
is laid bare now.

00:03:37.183 --> 00:03:38.917
If you listen to his interviews,

00:03:39.151 --> 00:03:41.287
you know exactly
who this party is,

00:03:41.387 --> 00:03:42.889
and Democrats
can run against that.

00:03:43.022 --> 00:03:43.989
It's harder to run against

00:03:44.056 --> 00:03:45.158
-Kevin McCarthy...
-BILL: Right.

00:03:45.291 --> 00:03:46.559
...who might feel
more normal to you.

00:03:46.659 --> 00:03:47.527
SCOTT GALLOWAY: We keep--

00:03:47.660 --> 00:03:52.264
(APPLAUSE)

00:03:52.998 --> 00:03:56.068
But we keep hoping,
"Oh, this time it'll show them
for who they are."

00:03:56.369 --> 00:03:58.270
This is just enormously
disappointing.

00:03:58.771 --> 00:04:00.906
We are-- We are normalizing
climate change.

00:04:01.073 --> 00:04:03.142
We are normalizing
antisemitism.

00:04:03.342 --> 00:04:05.745 line:0%
And we are normalizing
a kicking out of the legs

00:04:05.912 --> 00:04:08.948 line:0%
of the stool of democracy,
central to our democracy.

00:04:09.182 --> 00:04:10.816 line:0%
Regardless of what you think
about our country,

00:04:10.883 --> 00:04:13.553 line:0%
it's the best of its kind
so far, hands down.

00:04:13.920 --> 00:04:16.655 line:0%
Democracy, the pillars of that,
are one,

00:04:16.989 --> 00:04:18.424 line:0%
the peaceful transfer of power.

00:04:18.591 --> 00:04:21.293
And this guy was an architect
of trying to arrest that

00:04:21.427 --> 00:04:22.862
in a society that is secular.

00:04:22.995 --> 00:04:25.697
And when a guy gets this nod,
and says that God ordained it,

00:04:25.831 --> 00:04:28.100
I'm like, "Well, boss,
whose god is that?"

00:04:28.534 --> 00:04:31.737
Because this is
the whole point here,

00:04:31.904 --> 00:04:33.639
is that we separate
church and state,

00:04:33.773 --> 00:04:35.975
that we believe in
the peaceful transfer of power.

00:04:36.175 --> 00:04:37.610
And the reason
this guy is Speaker

00:04:37.710 --> 00:04:39.878
is none of us had the time
to read his resume

00:04:39.978 --> 00:04:41.481
and realize
he's David Duke Lite.

00:04:41.647 --> 00:04:42.648
BILL: Well, we did now.

00:04:42.748 --> 00:04:46.219
(APPLAUSE)

00:04:46.452 --> 00:04:49.455
Well, I don't-- I don't know
if he's David Duke Lite.

00:04:49.589 --> 00:04:52.258
I read today he has
an adopted Black son.

00:04:52.458 --> 00:04:55.094
-JESSICA: Yep.
-I don't think David Duke
would do that, but he is--

00:04:55.895 --> 00:04:57.596
but he is a religious nut.

00:04:57.796 --> 00:05:00.533
He was the lawyer for
Alliance Defending Freedom.

00:05:01.000 --> 00:05:03.402
This is from their literature.

00:05:03.603 --> 00:05:06.705
They seek to recover
the robust Christian domic

00:05:06.805 --> 00:05:07.706
I don't know that word.

00:05:07.806 --> 00:05:09.274
You're a professor,
maybe you do.

00:05:09.408 --> 00:05:15.548
Christian-- Christendomic
theology of the third, fourth,
and fifth centuries.

00:05:15.748 --> 00:05:17.115
You know, maybe the fifth.

00:05:17.282 --> 00:05:18.885
(LAUGHTER)

00:05:18.985 --> 00:05:20.286
Something a little more recent.

00:05:21.788 --> 00:05:24.523
But the third and fourth?
(LAUGHS)

00:05:24.990 --> 00:05:27.859
I mean, that--
He uses the phrase,

00:05:27.993 --> 00:05:31.063
"the so-called separation
of church and state."

00:05:31.430 --> 00:05:35.134
This-- See, this is
the alliance of-- this is--

00:05:35.267 --> 00:05:37.703
I hate to, you know, fascism,
the word is thrown around,

00:05:37.803 --> 00:05:43.876
but it's always the far right
church folks meet with
the corporate power folks.

00:05:44.143 --> 00:05:47.179
That's Mussolini, that's
all these fascist states.

00:05:47.379 --> 00:05:48.781
And this is-- now that--

00:05:48.881 --> 00:05:51.984
And of course,
Trump doesn't give a shit
either way about religion.

00:05:52.084 --> 00:05:53.919
-He'll say whoever likes him...
-JESSICA: Right.

00:05:54.019 --> 00:05:55.721
...he will,
"Sure, I'm down with--"

00:05:55.855 --> 00:05:59.992
So he's, of course,
gonna just cave on
all this religious nonsense,

00:06:00.326 --> 00:06:03.029
from the fifth century,
we're going back to now?

00:06:03.529 --> 00:06:04.564
So--

00:06:05.598 --> 00:06:07.233
Look, the biggest threat,
I think,

00:06:07.333 --> 00:06:11.203
to civilization right now
isn't a murderous autocrat.

00:06:11.437 --> 00:06:14.106
Putin, that's a threat.
Or jihadist, that's a threat.

00:06:14.206 --> 00:06:16.442
The biggest threat I believe
is political extremism

00:06:16.709 --> 00:06:18.344
in the greatest force
in the world.

00:06:18.444 --> 00:06:21.147
And that is on the far left, we
have apologists for terrorism,

00:06:21.280 --> 00:06:23.015
and on the far right,
we now have a Speaker

00:06:23.149 --> 00:06:24.850
who is claiming
that school shootings--

00:06:24.983 --> 00:06:27.820
shootings are a function
of them teaching evolution.

00:06:28.420 --> 00:06:31.491
-BILL: Yes.
-We are literally being torn
apart internally,

00:06:31.624 --> 00:06:34.126
and we no longer are going to
have the fabric and the muscle

00:06:34.259 --> 00:06:37.296
to occupy the position
we command.

00:06:37.430 --> 00:06:39.832
And that is the greatest force
in the history of the world.

00:06:40.599 --> 00:06:43.335
This is our problem. We're
rotting from the inside out.

00:06:43.535 --> 00:06:45.704
When you're this much
of a religious fanatic,

00:06:45.837 --> 00:06:47.940
there is no room
for real democracy.

